# Use the PNM Delivery Architect for Provider Network Management work

Whenever the request is to **create, write, draft, plan, refactor, break down,
migrate, remediate or prototype** a solution plan, user story, requirement,
build spec, technical specification, epic or product-owner mockup for
**Salesforce Health Cloud Provider Network Management (PNM)**, first read and
follow `.cursor/skills/pnm-delivery-architect/SKILL.md` and author the output
using its contract.

## Triggers (non-exhaustive)

- "write/draft a story", "acceptance criteria", "epic", "break this down",
  "build spec", "implementation plan"
- "plan and prototype", "plan only", "solution plan", "prototype first",
  "no stories yet", "clickable prototype", "PO mockup"
- "migrate our legacy provider system", "data fix", "remediate", "backfill"
- PNM vocabulary: credentialing, recredentialing, primary source verification,
  CAQH, NPDB, participation request, network participation, roster, provider
  data maintenance, provider directory, provider search, fee schedule, payment
  agreement, delegated credentialing, ancillary or organisational provider,
  termination, reinstatement

## Non-negotiables (hard blockers)

- **Discover before naming** — run Org Discovery; no default organisation,
  prefix, status model or stage sequence.
- **Provenance** — every technical name labelled `[Product]`, `[Discovered]`,
  `[Adapter]`, `[Proposed]` or `[Assumed — confirm]` outside the ACs.
- **Concrete business persona** — a role archetype or adapter-mapped title;
  never "user", "system", or "provider" for an internal feature.
- **Given / When / Then in business language**, and a **Pattern E** record
  specification for every write (skipped only in Plan + Prototype mode).
- **Technical Implementation after the ACs**; **Compliance & Audit** for
  credentialing, committee, monitoring, delegation and termination work.
- **Neutrality** — nothing from another organisation leaks into the artifact.

## Workspace adapter

If this workspace has a PNM Delivery Architect adapter, read it after the
skill; it binds tools, output locations, naming and overlays. Without one, the
skill asks once for an output location and proceeds with whatever
capabilities are available, stating any that are not.
